.TH MURAL-CONFIG 5 "August 22, 2026" "mural 0.1.0" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
mural-config \- mural wallpaper daemon configuration
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I $MURAL_CONFIG
.br
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/mural/config
.br
.I ~/.config/mural/config
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR murald (1)
reads a simple line-oriented
.B key = value
configuration file. Blank lines are ignored. Inline comments start with
.B #
or
.B ;
unless inside single or double quotes. Values may be quoted.
.PP
If
.B MURAL_CONFIG
is set, that exact file is used and must exist. Otherwise murald reads
.B $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/mural/config
or
.B ~/.config/mural/config
when present. Some settings also have environment overrides; those are listed
with the key.
.SH QUICK STRUCTURE
The config has four main groups:
.IP \(bu 2
Path, library, and render keys such as
.BR wall_dir ,
.BR favorite_weight ,
and
.BR scale_mode .
.IP \(bu 2
Transition profile keys:
.BR transition.NAME.FIELD .
These tune animation behavior.
.IP \(bu 2
Action keys:
.BR action.next ,
.BR action.back ,
and similar. These choose which transition profile each
.BR muralctl (1)
action uses.
.IP \(bu 2
Canvas cache keys:
.BR canvas.* .
These tune thumbnail generation shared by canvas transitions.
.PP
The similar-looking prefixes
.B transition.canvas.*
and
.B canvas.*
mean different things:
.IP \(bu 2
.B transition.canvas.*
configures the built-in
.B canvas
transition animation.
.IP \(bu 2
.B canvas.*
configures the thumbnail cache used by any canvas transition profile.
.SH COMMON EXAMPLE
.EX
wall_dir = ~/Pictures/wallpapers
state_dir = ~/.local/state/mural
quarantine_dir = ~/Pictures/wallpapers/.quarantine

favorite_weight = 4
max_history = 1000
scale_mode = fill

# Built-in transition profiles.
transition.push.duration_ms = 2000
transition.push.easing = linear
transition.push.mode = portal

transition.canvas.zoom_out_ms = 180
transition.canvas.pan_ms = 80
transition.canvas.zoom_in_ms = 260
transition.canvas.mode = clipped
transition.canvas.pan_axis = auto
transition.canvas.overview_scale = 0.33
transition.canvas.tile_count = auto
# Optional cap for auto mode:
# transition.canvas.max_tile_count = 48

# Canvas thumbnail cache.
canvas.thumbnail_max_edge = 1536
canvas.cache.backend = auto
canvas.cache.workers = 1
canvas.cache.memory_mib = 512

# Full-size target-image decode workers.
decode.full_workers = 2

# High-level action bindings.
action.next = push:up
action.back = push:down
action.shift_forward = push:left
action.shift_back = push:right
action.replace = cut
action.quarantine = cut
action.startup = cut
.EE
.SH PATH KEYS
.TP
.BI wall_dir " = PATH"
Top-level wallpaper library directory. Environment override:
.BR MURAL_WALL_DIR ,
then legacy
.BR WALL_DIR .
Default:
.IR ~/Pictures/wallpapers .
.TP
.BI state_dir " = PATH"
Persistent mural state directory. Environment override:
.BR MURAL_STATE_DIR .
Default:
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/mural
or
.IR ~/.local/state/mural .
.TP
.BI quarantine_dir " = PATH"
Directory used by
.BR "muralctl quarantine" .
Environment override:
.BR MURAL_QUARANTINE_DIR ,
then legacy
.BR QUARANTINE_DIR .
Default:
.I wall_dir/.quarantine
.
.SH LIBRARY KEYS
.TP
.BI favorite_weight " = INTEGER"
Shuffle-bag favorite weighting. A favorite is still part of the normal library,
but it appears this many total times in a rebuilt shuffle bag, making future
random selections choose it more often. Environment override:
.BR MURAL_FAVORITE_WEIGHT ,
then legacy
.BR FAVORITE_WEIGHT .
Default: 4.
.TP
.BI max_history " = INTEGER"
Maximum per-layout history length. Environment override:
.BR MURAL_MAX_HISTORY ,
then legacy
.BR MAX_HISTORY .
Default: 1000.
.SH RENDER KEYS
.TP
.BI scale_mode " = MODE"
Default scaling mode: one of
.BR fill ,
.BR fit ,
.BR center ,
or
.BR stretch .
Environment override:
.BR MURAL_SCALE_MODE .
Default:
.BR fill .
.TP
.BI decode.full_workers " = N"
Worker count for full target-image decodes. Defaults to 2 and is clamped to
available CPU parallelism, up to 32. Environment override:
.BR MURAL_DECODE_FULL_WORKERS .
.SH TRANSITION OVERVIEW
Mural separates transition behavior into profiles and actions.
.PP
A transition profile describes how an animation works. Built-in profile names
are
.BR cut ,
.BR fade ,
.BR world ,
.BR push ,
and
.BR canvas .
Custom profiles use the same namespace:
.BR transition.NAME.FIELD .
.PP
An action binding chooses the transition value used by a high-level command
when the command does not pass an explicit
.BR --transition .
For example:
.EX
transition.push.duration_ms = 900
transition.push.mode = portal
action.next = push:up
action.back = push:down
.EE
.PP
Here
.B push
is the built-in profile, and
.B :up
or
.B :down
only overrides the push direction for that action.
.SH BUILT-IN TRANSITION PROFILES
.SS Built-in fade profile
.TP
.BI transition.fade.duration_ms " = MS"
Fade transition duration in milliseconds. Default: 900.
.TP
.BI transition.fade.easing " = NAME"
Fade easing: one of
.BR linear ,
.BR ease-out-cubic ,
or
.BR ease-in-out-cubic .
Default:
.BR ease-out-cubic .
.SS Built-in push profile
.TP
.BI transition.push.duration_ms " = MS"
Push transition duration in milliseconds. Default: 900.
.TP
.BI transition.push.easing " = NAME"
Push easing: one of
.BR linear ,
.BR ease-out-cubic ,
or
.BR ease-in-out-cubic .
Default:
.BR ease-out-cubic .
.TP
.BI transition.push.mode " = NAME"
Push renderer mode: one of
.BR portal ,
.BR screen ,
or
.BR pan .
Default:
.BR portal .
.SS Built-in canvas transition profile
.TP
.BI transition.canvas.zoom_out_ms " = MS"
Canvas zoom-out phase in milliseconds. Default: 180.
.TP
.BI transition.canvas.pan_ms " = MS"
Canvas overview pan phase in milliseconds. Default: 80.
.TP
.BI transition.canvas.zoom_in_ms " = MS"
Canvas zoom-in phase in milliseconds. Default: 260.
.TP
.BI transition.canvas.mode " = NAME"
Canvas preview mode:
.BR clipped
uses the original screen-sized clipped tiles,
.BR morph
reveals actual wallpaper aspect ratios during zoom-out and clips again during
zoom-in,
.BR overlap
uses overlapping full-image thumbnails, and
.BR collage
uses the focus-centered full-thumbnail collage layout.
.BR span
treats outputs as viewports into one shared morph-style desktop canvas. Default:
.BR clipped .
.B collage
and
.B span
require
.BR "transition.canvas.walk = strip" .
Environment override:
.BR MURAL_CANVAS_MODE .
.TP
.BI transition.canvas.walk " = NAME"
Canvas walk order:
.BR paged
walks a bounded row/column canvas from top-left to bottom-right, then starts a
new page; and
.BR strip
uses the older centered infinite-right strip. Default:
.BR paged .
Environment override:
.BR MURAL_CANVAS_WALK .
.TP
.BI transition.canvas.pan_axis " = AXIS"
Canvas natural-order pan axis:
.BR auto ,
.BR horizontal ,
or
.BR vertical .
.B auto
uses horizontal order on landscape outputs and vertical order on portrait
outputs. Default:
.BR auto .
.TP
.BI transition.canvas.easing " = NAME"
Canvas easing: one of
.BR linear ,
.BR ease-out-cubic ,
or
.BR ease-in-out-cubic .
Default:
.BR ease-out-cubic .
.TP
.BI transition.canvas.overview_scale " = SCALE"
Canvas overview tile scale as a fraction of the output. Lower values zoom
farther out and require more preview tiles. Default:
.BR 0.333333 .
.TP
.BI transition.canvas.tile_count " = auto|N"
Automatic tile count or exact manual tile count. In auto mode, mural derives
the count from
.BR overview_scale ,
output size, and
.B pan_axis
so the current and next tiles can remain centered without exposing canvas
edges. Manual counts may show blank space if too low. Maximum:
.BR 256 .
Default:
.BR auto .
.TP
.BI transition.canvas.max_tile_count " = N"
Optional cap for
.B tile_count = auto .
Unset means no user cap, but the internal safety maximum still applies.
Maximum:
.BR 256 .
.SH NAMED TRANSITION PROFILES
Use a named profile when several actions should share the same settings, or
when a profile should not modify the built-in defaults.
.PP
Mural validates every defined profile at startup, including profiles not bound
to an action. Fields from another transition type and invalid mode/walk
combinations are errors. Built-in profile names cannot be retyped.
.PP
Every custom profile starts with:
.TP
.BI transition.NAME.type " = TYPE"
Profile type: one of
.BR cut ,
.BR fade ,
.BR world ,
.BR push ,
or
.BR canvas .
.PP
Then add fields that apply to that type:
.TP
.BI transition.NAME.duration_ms " = MS"
Duration for
.BR fade ,
.BR world ,
and
.B push
profiles.
.TP
.BI transition.NAME.easing " = NAME"
Easing for animated profiles: one of
.BR linear ,
.BR ease-out-cubic ,
or
.BR ease-in-out-cubic .
.TP
.BI transition.NAME.direction " = DIR"
Default push direction for push profiles when the action reference does not
supply one:
.BR up ,
.BR down ,
.BR left ,
or
.BR right .
.TP
.BI transition.NAME.mode " = NAME"
Push renderer mode for push profiles:
.BR portal ,
.BR screen ,
or
.BR pan .
Canvas preview mode for canvas profiles:
.BR clipped ,
.BR morph ,
.BR overlap ,
.BR collage ,
or
.BR span .
.TP
.BI transition.NAME.walk " = NAME"
Canvas walk order for canvas profiles:
.BR paged
or
.BR strip .
.TP
.BI transition.NAME.zoom_out_ms " = MS"
Canvas zoom-out phase in milliseconds for canvas profiles.
.TP
.BI transition.NAME.pan_ms " = MS"
Canvas overview pan phase in milliseconds for canvas profiles.
.TP
.BI transition.NAME.zoom_in_ms " = MS"
Canvas zoom-in phase in milliseconds for canvas profiles.
.TP
.BI transition.NAME.pan_axis " = AXIS"
Canvas natural-order pan axis for canvas profiles:
.BR auto ,
.BR horizontal ,
or
.BR vertical .
.TP
.BI transition.NAME.overview_scale " = SCALE"
Canvas overview tile scale for canvas profiles.
.TP
.BI transition.NAME.tile_count " = auto|N"
Automatic or exact manual tile count for canvas profiles. Maximum:
.BR 256 .
.TP
.BI transition.NAME.max_tile_count " = N"
Optional cap for automatic canvas tile counts. Maximum:
.BR 256 .
.TP
.BI transition.world.fallback " = cut|push:DIR"
Immediate fallback used when an existing
.B world
cache cannot cover a requested route. The fallback is only used for
route-gated world requests; a true no-cache startup failure still reports the
world cache command to run. DIR is
.BR up ,
.BR down ,
.BR left ,
or
.BR right .
.PP
Example:
.EX
transition.fast.type = push
transition.fast.duration_ms = 350
transition.fast.easing = ease-in-out-cubic
transition.fast.mode = pan

action.next = fast:up
action.back = fast:down
.EE
.SH ACTION TRANSITION KEYS
These keys choose the transition used by high-level
.BR muralctl (1)
wallpaper actions.
.TP
.BI action.next " = TRANSITION"
Default transition for
.BR "muralctl next" .
.TP
.BI action.back " = TRANSITION"
Default transition for
.BR "muralctl back" .
.TP
.BI action.shift_forward " = TRANSITION"
Default transition for forward shifts.
.TP
.BI action.shift_back " = TRANSITION"
Default transition for backward shifts.
.TP
.BI action.replace " = TRANSITION"
Default transition for replacements.
.TP
.BI action.quarantine " = TRANSITION"
Default transition for quarantine replacements.
.TP
.BI action.startup " = TRANSITION"
Startup display transition.
.SH TRANSITION VALUES
An action transition value is one of:
.TP
.B cut
Immediate cut.
.TP
.B fade
Blend the complete old and new wallpaper scenes using the built-in fade
profile.
.TP
.B canvas
The built-in canvas transition profile.
.TP
.BI canvas : AXIS
The built-in canvas profile with its pan axis overridden. AXIS is
.BR auto ,
.BR horizontal ,
or
.BR vertical .
.TP
.BI push: DIR
The built-in push profile with DIR set to
.BR up ,
.BR down ,
.BR left ,
or
.BR right .
.TP
.B NAME
A named transition profile.
.TP
.BI NAME : OVERRIDE
A named push profile with its direction overridden, or a named canvas profile
with its pan axis overridden.
.PP
The
.B canvas
transition is supported for high-level wallpaper actions. Low-level
.BR "muralctl set"
rejects canvas because it bypasses the history and shuffle state needed to
build a stable preview tape.
.B world
can be used by explicit
.BR "muralctl set"
requests because the supervisor derives route metadata from current renderer
health and the requested target paths.
.PP
Canvas starts with the current wallpaper centered, zooms out, pans along the
configured natural-order axis through layout history plus forward shuffle-bag
entries, then zooms in on the target wallpaper. Its preview can use the
original clipped tiles, morphing aspect-ratio tiles, overlapping full-image
thumbnails, a focus-centered collage, or a shared desktop-spanning morph
canvas. The focus-centered collage and desktop span modes
require
.BR "walk = strip" .
.SH CANVAS CACHE KEYS
These keys configure thumbnail generation and cache behavior shared by all
canvas transition profiles. They do not select or tune animation timings.
.TP
.BI canvas.thumbnail_max_edge " = PX"
Maximum cached thumbnail edge for canvas preview tiles. Defaults to 1536.
Higher values reduce overview blur but increase cache generation/upload cost.
Environment override:
.BR MURAL_CANVAS_THUMBNAIL_MAX_EDGE .
.TP
.BI canvas.cache.backend " = NAME"
Canvas thumbnail cache backend:
.BR auto ,
.BR vips ,
or
.BR internal .
.B auto
prefers
.BR vipsthumbnail
when available and falls back to the internal Rust decoder. Environment
override:
.BR MURAL_CANVAS_CACHE_BACKEND .
.TP
.BI canvas.cache.workers " = N"
Conservative background canvas cache worker count. Defaults to 1 and is
clamped to available CPU parallelism, up to 32. Explicit
.BR "muralctl cache warm --workers"
requests can schedule more worker threads for that request. Environment
override:
.BR MURAL_CANVAS_CACHE_WORKERS .
.TP
.BI canvas.cache.memory_mib " = N"
Decoded canvas thumbnail RAM cache size in MiB. Defaults to 512. This cache
stores decoded RGBA thumbnail pixels and reduces request-time disk decode
latency for large canvas overviews. Environment override:
.BR MURAL_CANVAS_CACHE_MEMORY_MIB .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR murald (1),
.BR muralctl (1),
.BR systemd.service (5)
